# Pulled platform reference — NOT source, and deliberately never committed.
# `octwin platform-kb pull` writes this from whatever platform you are pointed at, so a
# committed copy is a snapshot that goes stale the moment the platform moves. The Octwin
# Claude plugin ships no snapshot for the same reason: the KB is pulled, not bundled.
.octwin/

# Content-addressed staging the CLI writes while validating/deploying.
.pack-bundles/

node_modules/

# Internal engineering feedback on the platform + CLI — a candid list of our own bugs,
# gaps and workarounds, written for the platform team. Useful locally, not something to
# publish under the company org on a public repo. Delete this line to include it.
FEEDBACK.md

# Internal notes ABOUT the packs — the two counterparts to FEEDBACK.md above, and ignored for
# the same reason it is: this repo is public under the company org.
#
#   BACKLOG.md    — "you shipped this wrong", per pack, with file:line evidence and corrected YAML.
#   ENRICHMENT.md — what the platform grew and which packs should adopt it.
#
# Both are candid about our own packs, so they stay local. Delete a line to include it.
#
# They have their OWN reason here on purpose. They used to sit under a comment explaining
# `pack.json` (a per-developer deploy config, retired 2026-07-29), which left the only visible
# justification one that plainly did not apply to them — and a correct decision filed under the
# wrong reason reads as an accident. It was misread exactly that way on 2026-08-25, and nearly
# published a defect list for eleven packs.
ENRICHMENT.md
BACKLOG.md

# Playwright MCP scratch output (browser snapshots / console logs)
.playwright-mcp/
